---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Research">

  <h1>Research & Experiments</h1>

  <p style="opacity: 0.8; max-width: 750px;">
    I explore AI, machine learning, and distributed systems by rebuilding core research papers and systems from scratch.
    The goal is not just to use libraries, but to understand how real systems behave under the hood.
  </p>

  <!-- ========================= -->
  <!-- AI / ML PAPERS -->
  <!-- ========================= -->

  <section style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <h2>AI / ML Core Papers</h2>

    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; margin-top: 16px;">

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>Attention Is All You Need (Transformer)</h3>
        <p>Rebuilt scaled dot-product attention and multi-head mechanism to understand token interactions and context learning.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/transformer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>BERT: Masked Language Modeling</h3>
        <p>Implemented masked language modeling to understand bidirectional context learning in transformer models.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/bert-mlm" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>CLIP (Vision + Language Alignment)</h3>
        <p>Built contrastive learning pipeline for aligning image and text embeddings into a shared semantic space.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/clip-experiments" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>Batch Normalization</h3>
        <p>Reimplemented normalization layers to understand training stability in deep neural networks.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/batchnorm" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ========================= -->
  <!-- RETRIEVAL SYSTEMS -->
  <!-- ========================= -->

  <section style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <h2>Retrieval & Search Systems</h2>

    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; margin-top: 16px;">

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>FAISS / Vector Search Engine</h3>
        <p>Built approximate nearest neighbor search system for high-dimensional embeddings and semantic retrieval.</p>
        <img src="https://placehold.co/900x400" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin-top:10px;" />
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/vector-search" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ========================= -->
  <!-- DISTRIBUTED SYSTEMS -->
  <!-- ========================= -->

  <section style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <h2>Distributed Systems (Go / Java)</h2>

    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; margin-top: 16px;">

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>MapReduce (Google Paper)</h3>
        <p>Reimplemented simplified MapReduce pipeline using Go routines to simulate distributed computation.</p>
        <p style="opacity: 0.7;">Go: goroutines, worker pools, channel-based reducers</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/mapreduce-go" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>Raft Consensus Algorithm</h3>
        <p>Simulated leader election, log replication, and fault-tolerant distributed state machine.</p>
        <p style="opacity: 0.7;">Go / Java: concurrency, state machines, election timers</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/raft" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>Kafka-style Event Log System</h3>
        <p>Built append-only log system to understand streaming architecture and durability guarantees.</p>
        <p style="opacity: 0.7;">Go: producers, consumers, persistent logs</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/event-log" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ========================= -->
  <!-- SYSTEM DESIGN CORE -->
  <!-- ========================= -->

  <section style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <h2>Systems & Storage Engines</h2>

    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; margin-top: 16px;">

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>LSM Tree (Storage Engine)</h3>
        <p>Implemented log-structured merge tree to understand write-heavy database design (LevelDB-style systems).</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/lsm-tree" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

      <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>In-Memory KV Store (Redis-like)</h3>
        <p>Built key-value store with TTL, caching, and eviction policies for understanding backend systems.</p>
        <p style="opacity: 0.7;">Java: concurrency, caching, thread-safe storage</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/kv-store" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ========================= -->
  <!-- EXPERIMENTS -->
  <!-- ========================= -->

  <section style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <h2>Experiments</h2>

    <div style="padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #222; border-radius: 10px;">
      <h3>OCR + Video Frame Intelligence (FrameIQ)</h3>
      <p>
        Extracted video frames and built OCR + captioning pipeline to enable interaction with video content.
      </p>

      <img src="https://placehold.co/900x400" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin-top:10px;" />

      <a href="https://github.com/yourusername/frameiq" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
    </div>

  </section>

</Layout>